# Trading Safety

- MUST NOT execute orders directly from Telegram handlers.
- Order execution MAY exist only after parsing + validation + risk checks (future stages).
- MUST design for idempotency: duplicate Telegram events MUST NOT imply duplicate orders.
- Edited messages MUST NOT automatically create a second order.
- Stale signal validation MUST exist before any future live trading.
- Paper/testnet mode MUST appear before mainnet execution.
- Production/live trading MUST require explicit configuration; NEVER enable via hidden default.
- Every future execution MUST correlate to a stable event / correlation ID.
